1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,080
Listen to a talk on a history podcast.

2
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:11,180
In the 19th century, cities in the United States became crowded.

3
00:00:11,180 --> 00:00:16,150
Many businesses and apartments were housed in tall buildings.

4
00:00:16,150 --> 00:00:19,080
Fires became a major concern.

5
00:00:19,080 --> 00:00:24,210
Most firetruck ladders only reached the fourth floor, which wasn't high enough.

6
00:00:24,210 --> 00:00:28,163
Although laws were passed to require escape routes,

7
00:00:28,163 --> 00:00:31,100
many early ideas were impractical

8
00:00:31,860 --> 00:00:36,070
like one idea was to attach a parachute to your head.

9
00:00:36,070 --> 00:00:41,140
The parachute idea, well, this wouldn't work too well, would it?

10
00:00:41,140 --> 00:00:44,260
Other such ideas were met with resistance, too.

11
00:00:44,260 --> 00:00:52,110
Enter Anna Connolly, who received patents for fire escapes in the 19th century.

12
00:00:52,110 --> 00:00:55,272
Anna Connolly's initial fire escape design was a bridge

13
00:00:55,272 --> 00:01:00,894
so people could safely go up to the roof or upper floors of their own building,

14
00:01:00,894 --> 00:01:05,110
cross to the building next door, and go down the stairs there.

15
00:01:05,110 --> 00:01:10,150
This made good sense since most fires started on the lower floors of buildings.

16
00:01:10,150 --> 00:01:20,160
After this design, Connolly created another that was a series of platforms attached to the side of a building with ladders connecting them.

17
00:01:20,160 --> 00:01:27,100
She specified they'd be made of iron, since iron is fireproof and resists pressure.

18
00:01:27,100 --> 00:01:32,220
Well, this design worked, was practical, and was adopted across the country.

19
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:36,210
Connolly's fire escapes saved lives.

20
00:01:36,210 --> 00:01:39,963
These days, buildings in the US are built

21
00:01:39,963 --> 00:01:44,260
with interior stairwells that are fireproof for escape

22
00:01:44,360 --> 00:01:47,000
and are not visible from the outside.

23
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:54,020
But you can still see Connolly's design on older buildings in cities.
